//   - trans: Operation op(Q) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix C
//   - k: Number of elementary reflections whose product defines the matrix Q. If side is CUBLAS_SIDE_LEFT, m >= k >= 0; if side is CUBLAS_SIDE_RIGHT, n >= k >= 0
//   - a: array of dimension lda * k with lda is not less than max(1,m). The matrix A is from geqrf, so i-th column contains elementary reflection vector
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A. If side is CUBLAS_SIDE_LEFT, lda >= max(1,m); if side is CUBLAS_SIDE_RIGHT, lda >= max(1,n)
//   - tau: array of dimension k. The vector tau is from geqrf, so tau(i) is the scalar of the i-th elementary reflection vector
//   - c: array of size ldc * n. On exit, C is overwritten by op(Q)*C or C*op(Q)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array of matrix C. ldc >= max(1,m)
//   - work: Working space, array of size lwork
//   - lwork: Size of working array work
//   - devInfo: If devInfo = 0, the ormqr is successful. If devInfo = -i, the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle)
//
